menu "Knob shared UI (P1)"

config KNOB_UI_ENABLE
    bool "Link the shared clock UI (screens/settings) into the knob"
    default y
    help
        The P1 umbrella kill-switch. With y (the family posture) the knob
        boots the SHARED home screen (moon image + split-flap HH:MM +
        alarm row + seconds arc) through components/ui over the
        knob_moon_render.c seam. With n the knob keeps its K7
        own-screen moon view (disk + caption) and components/ui is not
        added to the build at all -- the plan's staged bring-up.

config KNOB_DIAG_TOUCH_INJECT_S
    int "Bench: inject a synthetic home tap at N seconds after boot (0 = off)"
    default 0
    help
        Bench-only crash-repro hook (the 2026-11-11 sweep-phase tap
        lockup): an esp_timer one-shot arms a ~350 ms synthetic press
        at (207,185) -- the crash's coordinates -- that flows through
        the real touch_read_cb exactly like a finger, so the repro is
        hands-free and needs no sweep caption on glass (the shared
        home screen never showed one). Production default 0 = dead.

config KNOB_DIAG_FRAME_TRACE
    bool "Bench: log flush/swap/screen-switch boundaries"
    default n
    help
        Bench-only: ESP_LOGI at flush start/complete, swap-task apply
        begin/end, sweep-abort, land_current_phase, and each leg of
        the fade + atomic screen switch, so a frozen board's LAST log
        line names the section that stuck.

config KNOB_DIAG_PANIC_AT_FRAME
    int "Bench: abort() after sweep frame N (0 = off) — black-box self-test"
    default 0
    help
        Bench-only witness-chain proof (task #27): abort() the producer
        after the N-th published sweep frame, so the boot after MUST
        print the gasp marker (stage/pub/applied) and the flash
        coredump must be readable with `idf.py -C knob coredump-read`.
        Proves the crash witness end to end without waiting for the
        unreproducible field crash. Production default 0 = dead.

endmenu
